From 2fa4f55aba1016f246c1247fb81b52a5605fcb87 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 78andyp <drandypowell@live.co.uk>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 20:01:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [VideoPlayer] Close the player controls when a Blu-ray opens
 a menu

The video OSD closes when the user opens the disc menu, but not when an
HDMV disc opens a menu itself, for example after its intro. The OSD then
takes the arrow keys that should move around the menu.

libbluray reports a BD-J menu when the disc first shows graphics,
usually at the start of the disc, and not again while those graphics
stay on screen, so on BD-J discs the OSD is only closed then.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoPlayer.cpp | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoPlayer.cpp b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoPlayer.cpp
index 219f03b..74a2ca3 100644
--- a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoPlayer.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoPlayer.cpp
@@ -5204,6 +5204,11 @@ int CVideoPlayer::OnDiscNavResult(void* pData, int iMessage)
         m_dvd.iDVDStillTime = 0ms;
         CLog::Log(LOGDEBUG, "BD_EVENT_MENU - libbluray leave menu (DVDSTATE_NORMAL)");
       }
+      else
+      {
+        // The disc may open a menu itself, so close the player controls as ShowVideoMenu does
+        CServiceBroker::GetAnnouncementManager()->Announce(ANNOUNCEMENT::Player, "OnMenu");
+      }
       break;
     case BD_EVENT_PLAYLIST_STOP:
       m_dvd.state = DVDSTATE_NORMAL;
